WHAT A GREEN RUN DOES AND DOES NOT MEAN:
  DOES  -- every documented opcode was executed and its result, flags and
           memory effect matched an independently written reference model,
           across all addressing modes including zero-page wrap, (zp),Y
           page carry and abs,X/Y indexing.
  DOES NOT -- prove the undocumented opcodes behave like NMOS silicon;
           prove cycle timing (that is cycletest);
           exhaust operand VALUES -- each opcode is tested at a handful of
           inputs chosen for their corners, not over all 2^16 combinations;
           or catch a misconception SHARED by the model and the CPU.
  So this is a strong breadth check, not a substitute for the Klaus
  Dormann suite, which exercises long dependent instruction sequences.

